---
code: K0018
title: Use Without Header
severity: ERROR
since: 0.1.0
category: parse
deprecated: False
tags: [parse, syntax, use, import, ffi, header]
description: "'use' declaration requires a plain header path string"
---

A `use` declaration must be followed by a plain string literal specifying the C header path to import (optionally followed by `as` and an alias). Bare identifiers or interpolated strings are not permitted.

## Example

This error occurs when `use` is followed by an unquoted identifier or an interpolated string:

```kura
use stdio.h

let dir = "include"
use "{dir}/math.h" as math
```

## Solution

Provide a plain, double-quoted string literal for the header path:

```kura
use "stdio.h" as c
use "include/math.h" as math
```
